<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  Which customer-data sections each InstaPay action makes stale.

  ===========================================================================
  THE BUG THIS FIXES: A RESTORED BASKET THAT THE MINICART NEVER HEARD ABOUT
  ===========================================================================
  Leaving the transfer page cancels the order and calls
  CheckoutSession::restoreQuote() (see Controller/Transfer/Cancel.php), so the
  shopper's items are genuinely back — and the cart PAGE, rendered server-side,
  showed them.

  The minicart did not. Magento serves the header counter and the drawer from
  `customer-data`, a localStorage cache, and the copy sitting there was the one
  written when the order was placed: empty. Nothing invalidated it, because
  invalidation is driven by THIS file — `Magento_Customer/js/customer-data`
  listens for form submits and asks `section-config` which sections the target
  URL affects. A custom route that is not listed affects nothing, so the stale
  empty cart survived the restore and every page load after it.

  That is the "cart page has my items but the drawer says it is empty" split.

  ===========================================================================
  `save` IS THE ONE THAT EMPTIES THE BASKET NOW
  ===========================================================================
  It was deliberately absent, on the reasoning that the quote had already been
  consumed by the time a receipt was uploaded. That is no longer true: the order
  is created BY that request (Controller\Transfer\Save), so submitting the
  receipt is the moment the basket goes — and the moment the cached minicart
  becomes a lie. Left unlisted, the shopper reached the success page with the
  old basket still in the header and only an add-to-cart shook it loose.

  ===========================================================================
  `cancel` IS NOW ALMOST ALWAYS A NO-OP, AND IS STILL LISTED
  ===========================================================================
  With no order created up front there is normally nothing to cancel and nothing
  to restore, so the basket does not change and this entry costs one comparison.
  It is kept for the legacy branch — an order placed by the previous behaviour,
  still `pending_payment`, which that controller does cancel and restore.

  Both actions also set Magento's own `section_data_clean` cookie server-side.
  That is not redundancy for its own sake: the matching below depends on
  `section-config` canonising the posted URL, and on this store the base URL
  carries a store code, which is exactly where that matching is thin.
-->
<config xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:module:Magento_Customer:etc/sections.xsd">
    <action name="spartrak_instapay/transfer/save">
        <!-- The order was just created from this quote: the header counter and
             the drawer are both stale from this request onwards. -->
        <section name="cart"/>
        <!-- The shipping and payment method chosen for a quote that no longer
             exists. Left behind, they are preselected on the next checkout. -->
        <section name="checkout-data"/>
        <!-- Magento_Checkout lists this alongside `cart` for its own
             order-placing action; the reorder block on the account dashboard
             reads it. -->
        <section name="last-ordered-items"/>
    </action>

    <action name="spartrak_instapay/transfer/cancel">
        <!-- The header counter and the drawer. -->
        <section name="cart"/>
        <!-- The checkout's own localStorage: the shipping method and payment
             method chosen for the order that has just been cancelled. Left
             behind, they are preselected against a quote that has been through
             a cancel-and-restore cycle. -->
        <section name="checkout-data"/>
    </action>
</config>
